#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# apply_sides

#% text
# `apply_sides(f, r)` applies `f` to both sides of the relation `r` (`==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`); a list of relations threads.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
apply_sides(f, a == b)
#% output
#= f(a) == f(b)

#% cell
apply_sides(sqrt, x^2 + 1 > 4)
#% output
#= (1 + x^2)^(1/2) > 2

#% cell
apply_sides(y => y^4, a == b)
#% output
#= a^4 == b^4

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `add_sides`, `multiply_sides`, `divide_sides`
